#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536948} :activity/id #uuid "5011f029-40b3-50ae-adc7-c8594e763c6a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049068 :topic/id #uuid "d78ca6bb-945f-51db-a4af-fc777024df22" :topic/math-academy-id 1459} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536917 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8113f0c1-13bf-5ab2-9884-6d72597b1b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$Q$ and $S$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109304} {:answer/id #uuid "8a8d835d-c354-5c3b-ad6e-6b19f2da5a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109305} {:answer/id #uuid "bee1b7de-ab86-59bc-81ce-c2ecde07ae92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109306} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa8a596-87e0-598e-9105-9841f4e811d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109307} {:answer/id #uuid "44b7bf2b-d86f-5d31-82a9-bbadefe43231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109308}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186109308} :answer-field/id #uuid "e044e866-6811-5b05-95ac-6974da60d777" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5b35d665-09e4-54b3-8c80-68318024b0ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-53035" :question/problem "![](images/70/702edb8e1ea4a79ea12e891ed3874c36ff3e6628c9cb000753f74ca7bc35ec74.png)\n\nWhich of the figures above is a parallelogram?" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a parallelogram is a quadrilateral with $2$ pairs of parallel sides.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is a rectangle. Therefore, its opposite sides are parallel, so it is a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a kite. It has a pair of opposite sides that are not parallel, therefore, it is not a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a rhombus. Since the opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel, it is a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $S$ is a trapezoid. It has only one pair of parallel sides, therefore, it is not a parallelogram.\n\nTherefore, shapes $P$ and $R$ are parallelograms. The shapes $Q$ and $S$ are not parallelograms."} :step/id #uuid "2cfe7fe6-dfad-5186-856c-597f87ad3a5e"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536937 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48305576-11d5-5617-960a-a3990bcb7dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536394} {:answer/id #uuid "5af8d66e-d7ec-5f20-b9b6-13fb2ff0d05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536443} {:answer/id #uuid "bfbf47b7-c34e-5794-aa4d-102f253c4306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536584} {:answer/id #uuid "f2464b38-1ef3-59d6-af91-e21eb614b53f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536670} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b0cf17-65c2-51ce-89a4-44437b972a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536677}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536443} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec71a978-52b7-54a3-b5fa-ef72f160c9d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55788c3c-c1d0-5ef8-8ff4-5e5fd3b4c618" :question/math-academy-id "q-53012" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e20dca5a916c43e93dd94b92ff4c1949a111537a8cb2e45b9ca0be7e2300f40.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the square above?\n\nI. $AB=BC=CD=AD.$\n\nII. $m∠ABC=m∠ADC.$\n\nIII. $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is parallel to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. A square is a rectangle where all sides are congruent, hence $AB=BC=CD=AD.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The angles in a square are all right. Therefore, $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}=m∠ADC.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Opposite sides of a square are parallel, and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is opposite $\\overset{―}{BC},$ therefore $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is parallel to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$\n\nIn conclusion, statements I, II, and III are true."} :step/id #uuid "6b24c0db-50fd-51da-9580-556fff1c0632" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536917}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536948 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24387f91-25bf-5714-8675-ef415eba960e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536337} {:answer/id #uuid "28dbcf41-1538-5429-b8d5-50fbfa182de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536344} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7da163-a580-5e50-a38f-f8e138ef74c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536510} {:answer/id #uuid "edec2c50-c3f2-5ae9-9a96-0ba69435f615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536661} {:answer/id #uuid "f02da5b5-90ef-5511-90c7-04d4ca4bf833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536664}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536510} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a514638-3f19-527b-a1de-1e926b7c8285" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "13987c3a-59aa-55ed-8fe6-1cb169d96b89" :question/math-academy-id "q-53009" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b0dd854ae2edb38245466049806c7e93bb4b704a03284905d968869fa1b4146.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the kite above?\n\nI. $AB=AD.$\n\nII. The kite has a pair of congruent opposite angles.\n\nIII. $AB=BC=CD=AD.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. A kite is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other. In the figure, we can see that $AB=AD.$\n\n- Statement II is true. A kite always has a pair of congruent opposite angles.\n\n- Statement III is false. A kite is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other. However, not all sides are congruent, for instance, $AB\\ne BC.$\n\nIn conclusion, statements I and II are true."} :step/id #uuid "866cff26-8806-5fb7-acaa-154a2dd5266d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536937}}] :activity/title "Classifying Quadrilaterals" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536273}]}
